From a589f08055db40214cf3d2dc282a1ed67faaf338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:23:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 039/240] Bugfix: agree on errors before entering collectives
 in large-count communication wrappers [report R. Perry]

In `commAllgatherv()`, `commGatherv()` and `commScatterv()`, which are
used when Gnum is wider than int, a process that found a count or
displacement that does not fit in an int, or that could not allocate
its conversion arrays, returned before entering the collective
communication, while the other processes entered it and waited
forever. The check on the local send count that was added to
`commGatherv()` in 73229e6 is also local to each process. Moreover,
the local count passed to `commAllgatherv()` and `commScatterv()` was
converted to int without any check, so that a count that does not fit
was silently truncated and the communication yielded wrong results
without any error.

Check the local count in the three routines, then agree on the error
status with an `MPI_Allreduce()` before calling the collective
communication routine, so that all processes return the same error
code. This adds one small collective communication per call, in
64-bit Gnum builds only.

Refs: COR-17, PS-COR-2
---
 src/libscotch/comm.c | 142 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 93 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/comm.c b/src/libscotch/comm.c
index d30d796..bf48ef4 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/comm.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/comm.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 /**    DATES     : # Version 5.1  : from : 30 jul 2010     **/
 /**                                 to   : 30 jul 2010     **/
